  "issues": [
    {
      "number": 3,
      "id": "I_kwDOKyF5GM6egyu7",
      "title": "qpack",
      "url": "https://github.com/kazuho/draft-kazuho-httpbis-http3-on-streams/issues/3",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "author": "LPardue",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "It was mentioned at the HTTP Workshop that using a reliable bytestream undervthe multiplexing changes some of the assumptions that QPACK over QUIC makes.\r\n\r\nOne suggestion was that setting the blocking limit to infinite may be beneficial.\r\n\r\nThis spec should probably have a QPACK considerations section",
      "createdAt": "2024-11-14T16:41:08Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-06-18T00:27:21Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-06-18T00:27:21Z",
      "comments": []
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "id": "I_kwDOKyF5GM8AAAABCVBxcw",
      "title": "Why is extended CONNECT a requirement?",
      "url": "https://github.com/kazuho/draft-kazuho-httpbis-http3-on-streams/issues/6",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "author": "LPardue",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "> Servers speaking HTTP/3 on Streams MUST implement the Extended CONNECT scheme defined in [[EXT-CONNECT3](https://kazuho.github.io/draft-kazuho-httpbis-http3-on-streams/draft-kazuho-httpbis-http3-on-streams.html#EXT-CONNECT3)].\n\nI can't recall why we added this, it seems a bit odd since the regular SETTINGS mechanism works. Forcing this feature would seem to add friction between HTTP/3 over QUIC and HTTP/3 over QMUX implementations: if you're a client MUST you always check for this extension and close the connection if unsupported? \n\nI think it would be easier to drop this",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-15T04:22:34Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-05-15T23:17:28Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-05-15T23:17:28Z",
      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "kazuho",
          "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
          "body": "I _think_ the intent is to avoid 1-RTT penalty when doing a 0-RTT resumption of an H3-over-QMux connection. Without such a requirement, a client cannot include an extended CONNECT request in the 0-RTT data, because the server might not advertise support for extended CONNECT on the resumed connection.\n\nThat said, I do not care either ways.",
          "createdAt": "2026-05-15T07:16:39Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-05-15T07:16:39Z"
        },
        {
          "author": "LPardue",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "body": "CONNECT is neither `safe` or `idempotent` (source: https://www.iana.org/assignments/http-methods/http-methods.xhtml)\n\nWhile I can see the potential advantage in the mandate, its seems to be trying to backdoor litigate on a broader issue related to extended CONNECT. \n\nI'd like to remove this for now for simplicity, we can reconsider it later on.",
          "createdAt": "2026-05-15T16:39:37Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-05-15T16:39:37Z"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
